  Text:
    m_Untranslated: This is the <b>Scene</b> view. Here, you'll view your 3D worlds
      and manipulate the things in them.<br><br>A <b>scene</b> is a simulated 3D
      space.
--- !u!114 &4472468033824496022
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: INSTRUCTIONS
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: '<b>1</b>.  Expand and watch the video above.


      <b>2</b>. 
      In the <b>Project</b> window, open the <b>Assets</b> > <b>Prefabs</b> folder.


      <b>Important</b>:
      Single-click, don''t double-click, <b>PlayerRobot</b> (<a href="https://learn.unity.com/tutorial/671be8afedbc2a0105a17c0e#671bf065edbc2a0105919b3b">Help</a>).


      <b>3</b>. 
      Drag the <b>PlayerRobot</b> asset from the <b>Project</b> window into the <b>Scene</b>
      view and onto the white ground in your scene.'
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
